    "brief_reference": "Improve the source portrait brightness, white balance, skin-tone naturalness and tonal relationships using image B only as an unaligned appearance guide. Image A is the source of identity, expression, gaze, facial geometry, readable text, objects, viewpoint and composition. Keep the source illumination geometry. Make only evidence-supported corrections to visible noise and blur. Do not reshape the face, whiten skin indiscriminately, smooth away natural skin texture, invent detail, or copy people, facial features, text or objects from image B.",
